    "Data": {
      "Ticketid": "HF-1001",
      "Customername": "Rita Alvarez",
      "Subject": "Locked out of my account",
      "Body": "Hi, I mistyped my password a few times this morning and now I'm locked out of everything including email. I also can't remember the exact password anymore. How do I get back in?",
      "Category": "Access",
      "Priority": "High",
      "Rationale": "KB article kb-01 directly covers password resets, lockout after failed attempts, mobile verification, password requirements, sync timing, and the service desk path if no mobile number is registered. The issue is Access because it concerns login/password lockout; priority is High because one user reports being locked out of all services including email.",
      "Confidence": 0.96,
      "Draftreply": "Hi Rita,\n\nI\u2019m sorry you\u2019re locked out after mistyping your password and can\u2019t remember the current one. You can reset your HomeFix network password from any browser, even off the network:\n\n1. Go to reset.homefixsupply.com.\n2. Enter your employee email and click \u201cSend verification code.\u201d\n3. Enter the 6-digit code sent to your registered mobile number.\n4. Choose a new password with at least 14 characters, including at least one number and one symbol. It cannot match your last 10 passwords.\n\nIf the account lockout was triggered after 5 failed attempts, it will clear automatically after 15 minutes. Once you reset the password, it should sync to email, VPN, and the HR portal within 5 minutes.\n\nIf you never registered a mobile number, the self-service reset will not work. Please call the IT service desk at extension 4357 so we can verify your identity and help you regain access.\n\nBest regards,\nHomeFix Supply Support Team"
    }
